cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "RNAseqLab: An Interactive Platform for RNA-seq Differential Expression and Functional Interpretation"
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: Yerushalmy
    given-names: Yonatan
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-2671-2457"

  - family-names: Amir
    given-names: Rachel

abstract: >-
  RNAseqLab is a local, interactive R Shiny platform for differential
  expression analysis and downstream biological interpretation of RNA-seq
  data. It integrates data import and quality assessment, differential
  expression testing, exploratory and publication-ready visualization,
  functional enrichment analysis, pathway analysis, gene annotation,
  specialized organism-specific analyses, and automated report generation
  within a unified workflow. The application accepts differential-expression
  results, raw count matrices, and transcript-quantification outputs generated
  by RSEM, featureCounts, Salmon, or Kallisto. By combining established
  bioinformatics methods with an accessible graphical interface, RNAseqLab
  enables researchers to perform reproducible downstream RNA-seq analyses
  locally without requiring command-line programming.

keywords:
  - RNA-seq
  - differential expression
  - R Shiny
  - DESeq2
  - functional enrichment
  - bioinformatics

repository-code: "https://github.com/Yo-yerush/RNAseqLab"

license: GPL-3.0-only

version: 0.9.2
date-released: "2026-07-27"